    "long_instructions": "## **Modify: Debug**\r\n\r\nAnother crew tried to get the painter to the cone, but their code has a bug. Find it and fix it so the painter finishes the job.\r\n\r\n1. Run the code and see what happens.\r\n2. Compare where the painter ends up to where the traffic cone is.\r\n3. Trace the code and find the bug in the code and fix it.\r\n4. Run again to check your fix.",
    "start_sources": {
      "files": {
        "0": {
          "id": "0",
          "name": "main.py",
          "contents": "# Set up painter commands\nfrom neighborhood import *\n\n# Sets the amount of paint for the painter\nset_paint(17)\n\n# The painter starts top left corner, facing the food truck\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nturn_left()\nturn_left()\nturn_left()\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nturn_left()\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nturn_left()\nturn_left()\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nturn_left()\nturn_left()\nturn_left()\nmove()\npaint(\"white\")\nturn_left()",
